WEBVTT

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:06.290
The number of Sekirei we've set free is 108.

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:11.480
And now the last one has spread and flapped its wings of light!

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:17.490
Finally, all the flags of the game's second stage have risen!

00:00:17.490 --> 00:00:21.570
Now, flap your wings towards the night of the gods!

00:00:21.890 --> 00:00:24.920
Towards that beautiful battlefield!

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:39.210
atarashii yakusoku ga kokoro wo tsuyoku tsunagu

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:39.210
Our new promise binds our hearts together strongly

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:46.300
kawaru sekai ni kane ga hibiku yukou

00:00:39.550 --> 00:00:46.300
The bell rings in the changing world, let's go

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:53.140
owari naki tatakai ga subete wo hiki saitemo

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:53.140
Even if the endless fight shreds everything apart,

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:59.320
kimi no hohoemi tada shinjite

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:59.320
I will believe in your smile

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.530
kimi no yume mamoreru nara

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.530
If I can protect your dream,

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.120
itami sae dakishimeyou

00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:07.120
I will even embrace pain

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:16.420
kasane au kono omoi mune no chikai yuzurenai

00:01:07.370 --> 00:01:16.420
I can't let go of these piling feelings, this oath in my heart

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:23.170
aa, sora no haruka hate made

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:23.170
Ah, all the way to the end of the sky,

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:31.390
sou, kakete yuku you na kasoku shiteku jounetsu

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:27.970
yes, my passion accelerates

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:31.390
as if it were rushing through my body

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:37.560
aa, donna unmei datte

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:37.560
Ah, no matter what kind of fate awaits me,

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:48.700
sou, takaku koeteku makenai yuuki kureta kara

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:41.860
yes, I can fly high over it

00:01:41.860 --> 00:01:48.700
because you gave me this undefeatable courage

00:01:57.690 --> 00:01:59.920
Looks like it's already over, doesn't it?

00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:05.380
At the very least, I wanted to check whether it was Kuu-chan or not!

00:02:05.380 --> 00:02:08.800
Dammit! It's all because of that moron on a bike!

00:02:10.570 --> 00:02:11.600
That guy...

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:12.580
Huh?

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:14.640
He was probably an Ashikabi.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:17.050
An Ashikabi? Him?

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:20.060
Yes. I'm not exactly sure, though.

00:02:20.060 --> 00:02:23.390
Then I guess he came here to wing the last one as well.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:24.820
That's a possibility.

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:32.240
Um...

00:02:32.240 --> 00:02:35.790
Do you still want to... kill president Minaka?

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:42.350
What would you do if I said I still do?

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:47.060
You've got your own feelings about this matter, don't you?

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:50.680
I don't have the right to stop you.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:55.850
However, right now, I want to return to Izumo Inn, and I want you to come with me.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:59.690
I don't want to see a comrade die a meaningless death.

00:03:03.260 --> 00:03:04.360
I won't go...

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.530
Or at least not for now.

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:12.410
I'm still kind of frustrated by the fact that I got winged by a man...

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:14.450
I-Is that so?

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:15.750
Minato-san!

00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:17.120
Kagari-chan!

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:20.620
Comrades, huh?

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:24.670
Sahashi Minato.

00:03:25.050 --> 00:03:27.340
I think I finally understand...

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:31.510
the reason why my body is reacting to you.

00:03:32.260 --> 00:03:33.350
Kagari-san?

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:34.680
Kagari-san!

00:03:34.680 --> 00:03:37.320
Get a hold of yourself, Kagari-san!

00:03:35.250 --> 00:03:40.350
I'm quite shocked, but I think I finally understand, Minaka.

00:03:41.810 --> 00:03:44.930
The importance of an Ashikabi to a Sekirei, that is...

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:53.900
Ouch. Where am I?

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:59.060
Oh, so you're finally awake, Kagari-san.

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:00.120
Miya...

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:05.940
Musubi-san carried you all the way here when you fainted on that roof the day before yesterday.

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.330
The day before yesterday?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:09.260
Then I've been out cold for two days...

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:11.240
Don't worry.

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:12.920
I was the one who treated your wounds.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.850
I wouldn't let that perverted animal touch you.

00:04:15.960 --> 00:04:18.480
Miya... I'm...

00:04:18.480 --> 00:04:20.810
Welcome home, Homura.

00:04:21.170 --> 00:04:25.390
Whatever the reason you left might have been, you've returned home.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:28.050
That alone makes me happy.

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.970
That's why I won't ask you any questions.

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:36.000
You really are like a mother.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.990
How rude.

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:40.830
I don't look that much older than the rest of you, you know...

00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:44.310
I'm back. Back from the dead.

00:04:45.540 --> 00:04:48.150
I'm sure that guy over there would be quite relieved to hear that, too.

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:52.380
He's been watching over you this whole time.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:59.510
Oh? Are you all right, Kagari-san?

00:05:00.060 --> 00:05:02.270
You know, you suddenly collapsed and all...

00:05:03.440 --> 00:05:04.940
I'm fine now.

00:05:05.890 --> 00:05:07.290
Um...

00:05:07.290 --> 00:05:10.170
My bandages are all soaked with sweat and it feels really uncomfortable...

00:05:10.600 --> 00:05:12.180
Would you mind changing them for me?

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:13.610
N-Not really...

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:18.480
Let's see... Bandages and the ointment...

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:20.620
The hell?!

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:23.650
Uh-! On second thought, I can't do this!

00:05:23.650 --> 00:05:25.460
H-Hold on a second! I'll get the Landlady right away!

00:05:26.770 --> 00:05:28.940
Since we've come this far...

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:31.000
I guess I've got no choice but to tell you...

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.610
You might have noticed already,

00:05:34.610 --> 00:05:37.470
but I'm different from all the other Sekirei.

00:05:37.900 --> 00:05:42.890
To subordinate myself, even my gender can be changed at the will of my Ashikabi.

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:47.400
I'm not even allowed to live for my own sake.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:50.020
In other words, Sahashi Minato,

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:52.910
my body will become what you desire it to be.

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:54.940
So...

00:05:55.860 --> 00:05:57.080
What do you think?

00:06:00.940 --> 00:06:04.790
Kagari san, breasts like those are poisonous for a virgin.

00:06:04.790 --> 00:06:07.310
All right, I'm going to apply the ointment.

00:06:07.310 --> 00:06:10.130
Sahashi, I'm trying to have a serious talk here...

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:15.340
What I desire is that you remain yourself, and nothing else.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:17.840
You're fine the way you are.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:19.920
And you should stay like that.

00:06:21.410 --> 00:06:23.550
Thank you, Sahashi.

00:06:24.660 --> 00:06:27.590
Then, I'll let you get some more rest, okay?

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:34.380
Why are they all sleeping in the corridor?

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:38.280
Ah, Minato-san...

00:06:39.050 --> 00:06:40.700
We were worried about Kagari-san.

00:06:42.640 --> 00:06:44.970
Kagari-san seems to be doing fine now.

00:06:45.410 --> 00:06:47.040
Oh, thank goodness.

00:06:47.040 --> 00:06:49.970
We can finally collect the rent, right?

00:06:49.970 --> 00:06:51.660
"Collect the rent," you say...?

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:54.200
Minato!

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:58.140
You didn't do anything indecent with Homura in there, did you?

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.090
I-I didn't do anything! Jeez...

00:07:00.090 --> 00:07:02.990
Really? So nothing happened?

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:03.760
Matsu-san!

00:07:03.760 --> 00:07:08.680
Just think about it: our Homura-tan approaching you with naked breasts just like that...

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:10.420
Nooo!

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:13.310
Burning me out of the blue...

00:07:13.310 --> 00:07:16.750
I see. Homura will do just fine then.

00:07:16.750 --> 00:07:17.440
Yup.

00:07:18.150 --> 00:07:20.660
Anyway, I'm relieved.

00:07:21.200 --> 00:07:26.830
He really might have died if his powers didn't stabilize.

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:30.160
Mina-tan saved his life by winging him.

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:31.250
Matsu.

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:34.920
Homura's been winged, and Minato has increased the number of his Sekirei.

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:39.340
Weren't you the one eager to expand the party when I became winged?

00:07:39.340 --> 00:07:42.300
Everything went exactly as you planned.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:43.780
Am I right?

00:07:45.220 --> 00:07:48.190
No, not really.

00:07:48.540 --> 00:07:53.970
Mina-tan's power as an Ashikabi far exceeded my expectations.

00:07:54.860 --> 00:07:58.030
So why is it that we need so much fire power?

00:07:58.580 --> 00:07:59.990
Answer me, Matsu!

00:07:59.990 --> 00:08:02.700
Just how much do you know about the Sekirei Project?

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:05.340
Matsu-san,

00:08:07.700 --> 00:08:11.040
I don't think I can be of any use the way I am right now.

00:08:11.040 --> 00:08:16.510
I don't know anything about the Ashikabi or the Sekirei.

00:08:16.930 --> 00:08:21.920
Even during our escape plan, I put Musubi-chan and everyone else in danger.

00:08:21.920 --> 00:08:23.380
This time as well,

00:08:23.380 --> 00:08:26.640
the moment we approached Kagari-san, the battle had begun.

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:31.480
I've already had enough of this. Making all of you fight without even knowing the reason...

00:08:31.930 --> 00:08:34.400
So please, Matsu-san, I want you to tell me.

00:08:34.790 --> 00:08:36.550
Tell me everything you know about the Sekirei Project.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:43.280
It seems you've finally found a way to use my abilities.

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:48.470
I, Sekirei No. 02 Matsu, will grant the request of my Ashikabi.

00:08:50.690 --> 00:08:53.010
I see, so Uzume-san is...

00:08:53.250 --> 00:08:56.970
Others didn't realize it yet, and I even managed to hide it from them as well,

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.150
but you know...

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:01.810
It's the path she's chosen for herself.

00:09:02.240 --> 00:09:04.860
I can do nothing but await her return.

00:09:05.430 --> 00:09:07.010
But you're fine with that, aren't you?

00:09:10.930 --> 00:09:12.390
Well then, Mina-tan,

00:09:12.390 --> 00:09:14.810
where would you like me to start?

00:09:16.230 --> 00:09:18.190
T-Tell me everything.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:21.490
I know the Sekirei Project is a secret plan,

00:09:21.490 --> 00:09:24.190
and that danger awaits whoever learns the whole truth.

00:09:24.190 --> 00:09:27.740
Still, upon my resolve as an Ashikabi...

00:09:27.740 --> 00:09:30.420
I've made my decision.

00:09:32.330 --> 00:09:36.940
It's all right. Should anything ever happen, I'll protect you.

00:09:36.940 --> 00:09:38.060
Musubi-chan...

00:09:38.380 --> 00:09:39.940
You're useless...

00:09:39.940 --> 00:09:41.880
Tsu-Tsukiumi...

00:09:42.380 --> 00:09:44.580
And you call yourself my Ashikabi?

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:47.550
No matter what dangers there might be, you have nothing to fear.

00:09:47.550 --> 00:09:49.340
Kuu's here for you, too.

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:51.340
Thanks a lot, Kuu-chan.

00:09:51.340 --> 00:09:53.230
Mina-tan!

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:55.480
Did you come here just to flirt around?

00:09:55.480 --> 00:09:58.650
Or are you going to listen to what I have to say?

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:00.230
Sorry, sorry...

00:10:00.230 --> 00:10:02.900
Everything... is what you said, right?

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:04.570
Very well.

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:08.530
This might take a little while to explain though.

00:10:10.350 --> 00:10:16.960
2 years ago, a mysterious island suddenly appeared out of nowhere along the Japanese coastlines.

00:10:17.400 --> 00:10:21.840
A couple of young students travelled out to this island and started its exploration.

00:10:21.840 --> 00:10:26.760
This is where the absurd story of the Sekirei Project began.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:30.690
This island soon became known as Kamikura Island.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:30.690
TL Note: Kamikura means God's treasury.

00:10:30.690 --> 00:10:34.680
What they discovered here were massive ruins that resembled a spaceship.

00:10:35.240 --> 00:10:39.230
Within these ruins, they discovered what they believed to be a great treasure, now known as Overtechnology.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:47.070
One of the students soon gained worldwide fame as an eccentric prodigy.

00:10:47.070 --> 00:10:53.240
He, Minaka Hiroto, had used the remains of the Overtechnology and established a large company for himself.

00:10:53.240 --> 00:10:57.540
But you already know this much, don't you?

00:10:57.540 --> 00:10:59.420
Ah, I do.

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:02.460
The large company he established was M.B.I.

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:07.490
Correct. What they found was a spaceship,

00:11:07.490 --> 00:11:11.950
and what this ship contained were 108 slumbering life forms.

00:11:12.260 --> 00:11:15.040
108? Does that mean...?

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:19.100
Yes, those life forms were us, the Sekirei.

00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:27.440
By the Sekirei, you mean you Sekirei...?

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:31.140
Oh my, that really is absurd.

00:11:31.140 --> 00:11:32.910
Should <i>you</i> really be saying that?

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:35.160
Oh, are you fine already?

00:11:35.160 --> 00:11:36.600
Thanks for your concern.

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:39.590
It's all thanks to Minato's nursing, you know.

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:42.330
Oh, it's love, isn't it? The power of love!

00:11:42.710 --> 00:11:45.460
That's right, by Sekirei I mean Sekirei.

00:11:43.880 --> 00:11:47.800
Isn't this... Matsu's wiretap speaker?

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.760
You've got a really bad habit of eavesdropping on people.

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:55.220
Oh, but this is just Duck-san who likes to talk about other people's secrets.

00:11:55.220 --> 00:11:59.940
And I'm just a young, beautiful, and ordinary landlady.

00:12:01.360 --> 00:12:03.140
Please stop that, Miya...

00:12:03.140 --> 00:12:06.480
We don't need to worry though,
Matsu won't say anything unnecessary.

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:10.320
Yup, everyone values their own lives after all.

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:16.880
That's right. If they came to know something they shouldn't, they might not be able to stay here any longer.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:18.390
That would be quite pitiful, wouldn't it?

00:12:18.390 --> 00:12:22.060
A man and his six Sekirei sleeping on the side of the road...

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:26.290
You're seriously scary...

00:12:26.290 --> 00:12:27.490
Let's continue.

00:12:27.490 --> 00:12:30.770
There were 108 Sekirei in slumber inside of the ship.

00:12:30.770 --> 00:12:32.410
One of them was a full-grown adult.

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:34.090
Eight of them were in an embryonic state.

00:12:34.090 --> 00:12:38.260
And the remaining 99 were all in the form of an egg.

00:12:38.260 --> 00:12:40.320
One and eight...

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:44.580
Then, the single digit numbers the Disciplinary Squad were talking about...!

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:45.840
Indeed,

00:12:45.840 --> 00:12:49.440
the single digit numbers are the Sekirei found either full-grown or as embryos.

00:12:49.440 --> 00:12:53.950
These Sekirei were mischievously altered much more than the others.

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:56.490
Musubi and mischievous!

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:57.370
What are you two implying?

00:12:57.410 --> 00:13:03.580
And so, all the Sekirei were adjusted into their current forms and then released.

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:05.270
Adjusted?

00:13:05.770 --> 00:13:09.250
Musubi got adjusted by Takami-san.

00:13:09.250 --> 00:13:11.370
So that's what she meant...

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:12.880
Oh, now I get it!

00:13:13.580 --> 00:13:20.070
Adjusting those who had already started to mature would be a much different process than altering those still in the egg form.

00:13:20.070 --> 00:13:22.810
Exactly, well thought out.

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:25.890
Therefore, being altered more doesn't necessarily mean to be made stronger than the rest.

00:13:23.150 --> 00:13:26.770
Mischievous, mischievous...

00:13:25.890 --> 00:13:29.320
The adjustments made would differ a lot, depending on each editor...

00:13:29.510 --> 00:13:31.820
Don't talk about the editors!

00:13:31.820 --> 00:13:34.260
I don't want to remember it!

00:13:34.260 --> 00:13:36.580
Scary... Just scary...

00:13:36.580 --> 00:13:38.780
My editor was Takami-san.

00:13:38.780 --> 00:13:40.130
Mine, too!

00:13:40.130 --> 00:13:44.420
Well, some editors managed to traumatize their Sekirei...

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:46.500
By the way, my editor was Takehito-tan.

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:48.420
Takehito-san...

00:13:49.010 --> 00:13:50.340
You mean the Landlady's husband?

00:13:52.300 --> 00:13:55.610
Most of the single digit numbers were adjusted by Asama Takehito,

00:13:55.610 --> 00:13:59.880
the other so-called prodigy within M.B.I.'s ranks.

00:14:00.390 --> 00:14:02.340
He also altered the adult,

00:14:02.340 --> 00:14:05.370
which, strictly speaking, wasn't really a Sekirei...

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:06.980
Not really a Sekirei?

00:14:06.980 --> 00:14:10.630
Ah, never mind! Just forget about that!

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:10.630
Oh, her tongue slipped.

00:14:11.940 --> 00:14:13.230
I guess she doesn't value her life after all.

00:14:13.230 --> 00:14:17.180
P-Putting that matter aside,

00:14:17.180 --> 00:14:20.370
let me tell you about an incident which occurred before M.B.I. grew to its current state.

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:23.450
An incident which threatened the life of all Sekirei:

00:14:23.830 --> 00:14:25.880
The invasion of Kamikura Island.

00:14:29.290 --> 00:14:35.860
Minaka Hiroto registered the island as his own private property and went as far as removing it from the world map.

00:14:35.860 --> 00:14:40.550
However, keeping such a thing secret from the rest of the world proved to be impossible.

00:14:41.040 --> 00:14:43.920
Then one day, something finally happened.

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:49.680
The troops of an unknown army invaded Kamikura Island.

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:52.270
Invasion...

00:14:52.770 --> 00:14:55.480
You were still asleep at that time, Homura-chan.

00:14:55.480 --> 00:14:58.640
M.B.I. didn't have its own army yet,

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:01.720
and only five Sekirei were prepared for battle.

00:15:01.720 --> 00:15:03.740
But we had to do what we could.

00:15:03.740 --> 00:15:07.250
And that's their origin:

00:15:07.780 --> 00:15:10.730
The S. Project's Guardians, The Disciplinary Squad.

00:15:10.710 --> 00:15:13.570
Naturally, the invasion lasted for an extended period of time,

00:15:13.570 --> 00:15:17.670
but the first attack wave was by far the strongest one.

00:15:18.360 --> 00:15:23.250
The original purpose of the Disciplinary Squad was the defence of the island.

00:15:23.740 --> 00:15:29.770
Its members were the numbers 1 through 5, with No. 01 as their leader.

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:35.230
Asama Takehito also provided special adjustment to these Sekirei,

00:15:35.230 --> 00:15:39.190
which is where the rumours of the single digits originated from...

00:15:41.320 --> 00:15:42.460
What is it?

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:45.340
The Disciplinary Squad?!

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:47.840
Yes, I was in it too.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.620
Is it really that surprising?

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:52.830
My adjustments are perfect.

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:55.420
You're now as powerful as winged Sekirei.

00:15:55.420 --> 00:15:58.640
No, you might be even stronger than that.

00:15:59.020 --> 00:16:02.380
Go, protect the children and the eggs.

00:16:02.380 --> 00:16:04.800
Oh, what a pain...

00:16:04.800 --> 00:16:07.310
These invasions come around quite often, don't they?

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:08.990
Stop complaining.

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:11.230
By the way, you stink of sake.

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:13.010
An army of unknown origin?

00:16:14.290 --> 00:16:17.190
I, No. 02, will find out who they are.

00:16:18.320 --> 00:16:20.190
I'm amazed.

00:16:20.190 --> 00:16:24.400
Usually we do nothing but fight,
but at times we stand together like this.

00:16:25.400 --> 00:16:30.130
Are you talking about us or the army that's attacking us?

00:16:30.690 --> 00:16:34.430
You guys, cut the chatter.

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:39.840
Many of our kin sleep behind our backs.

00:16:40.340 --> 00:16:41.690
Got it.

00:16:42.210 --> 00:16:43.300
Well then,

00:16:43.300 --> 00:16:45.400
I'll be making the first move.

00:16:46.090 --> 00:16:48.390
Access Search!

00:16:51.880 --> 00:16:53.490
Enemy armour division:

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:59.540
Helicopters: 12. Tanks: 15. Vessels: 2. Escort vessels: 1.

00:16:59.540 --> 00:17:02.860
Well, these numbers shouldn't pose any problem for us.

00:17:03.110 --> 00:17:04.770
Flower Whirlwind.

00:17:10.870 --> 00:17:11.660
Heavenly Crush.

00:17:23.720 --> 00:17:24.950
That's not very nice.

00:17:24.950 --> 00:17:29.560
Once you've set your feet upon this island, trying to run away is futile.

00:18:09.910 --> 00:18:11.460
It's already over, eh?

00:18:11.460 --> 00:18:13.310
Yes, total annihilation.

00:18:13.310 --> 00:18:15.010
Truly marvellous.

00:18:15.010 --> 00:18:18.150
Leaving the adjustment process to you was indeed a good decision.

00:18:19.080 --> 00:18:22.170
Right. Though, I'm surprised...

00:18:22.510 --> 00:18:24.230
This doesn't feel like much of a victory.

00:18:24.920 --> 00:18:28.030
I was so excited to learn more about Overtechnology,

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:31.120
thinking that I might be able to create something greater than humanity...

00:18:31.620 --> 00:18:34.540
But in the end, our actions are no different from regular humans.

00:18:35.040 --> 00:18:36.210
Is that so?

00:18:36.210 --> 00:18:38.370
I, on the other hand, am thrilled!

00:18:38.370 --> 00:18:40.810
Many people died today.

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:45.340
They deserved it. They spat towards heaven.

00:18:45.810 --> 00:18:47.760
That's all there is to it.

00:18:52.390 --> 00:18:55.810
Anyway, Asama-kun, I've just thought of something wonderful!

00:18:56.250 --> 00:19:03.230
Let us introduce an age of gods, a legend of miracles into this world!

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:05.650
Kagari-san...

00:19:05.650 --> 00:19:08.360
Why are you hiding all of a sudden?

00:19:08.360 --> 00:19:12.120
Well, this is the first time I've heard you can sink battleships...

00:19:12.120 --> 00:19:16.180
The Sekirei Project, known as the S. Project at the time,

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:18.540
took a drastic change of direction.

00:19:18.980 --> 00:19:24.980
Its original purpose was to secure the safety of those found in the spaceship, and to conduct research on them...

00:19:26.190 --> 00:19:28.990
Matsu-san was in the Disciplinary Squad...?

00:19:29.550 --> 00:19:30.960
You're all overreacting.

00:19:31.010 --> 00:19:32.290
I'm sorry.

00:19:32.600 --> 00:19:35.850
But why did you quit the Disciplinary Squad?

00:19:35.850 --> 00:19:39.390
Um, I didn't exactly quit...

00:19:39.390 --> 00:19:40.350
Rather, I ran away...

00:19:40.350 --> 00:19:41.610
Ran away?!

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:48.100
Well, I already told you so, didn't I? I'm on the run from M.B.I.

00:19:46.880 --> 00:19:48.100
Now that I think about it...

00:19:48.360 --> 00:19:50.120
why did <i>you</i> quit, Kazehana?

00:19:50.820 --> 00:19:52.780
I'm so glad you asked.

00:19:52.870 --> 00:19:56.160
President Minaka dumped me, so I set out on a journey to recover from the shock.

00:19:56.160 --> 00:19:59.750
And somewhere along the way, it became a journey to indulge myself with sake.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:01.670
I shouldn't have asked.

00:20:02.740 --> 00:20:04.590
Sahashi-san must be having a hard time,

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:06.740
being surrounded by such twisted Sekirei...

00:20:06.740 --> 00:20:08.640
Wha- Wait, Miya!

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:11.080
I'm also one of his Sekirei, remember?

00:20:11.080 --> 00:20:12.550
There's something else I'd like to ask...

00:20:12.550 --> 00:20:14.340
What happened to No. 05?

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:20.740
One day, he just stood up and left without any explanation.

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:25.380
I never thought he'd end up as one of the Mikogami of the South's.

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:28.320
People have their own problems, and so do Sekirei.

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:29.990
Musubi-chan...

00:20:29.990 --> 00:20:32.300
There's 108 of us after all.

00:20:32.640 --> 00:20:34.740
Uzume-san said something like that.

00:20:34.920 --> 00:20:36.830
People have their problems, huh?

00:20:36.830 --> 00:20:38.950
That does sound like something she would say.

00:20:41.210 --> 00:20:44.080
Didn't I tell you already? Uzume no longer exists.

00:20:44.460 --> 00:20:47.540
We might have to fight Uzume-tan at some point.

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:49.910
F-Fight Uzume-san?!

00:20:49.910 --> 00:20:53.840
Mina-tan, you said you were prepared and resolute about your decision earlier, right?

00:20:53.840 --> 00:20:55.930
Well... I did.

00:20:56.470 --> 00:21:01.870
That also means that you have the will to fight.

00:21:02.770 --> 00:21:08.440
With Homura-tan finally getting winged, the second stage of the Sekirei Project has some to an end.

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:12.340
At this point, we should wait for the president to make his next move.

00:21:12.340 --> 00:21:14.110
Sorry, I've got a message.

00:21:16.030 --> 00:21:18.870
Minaka... Hiroto?!

00:21:19.490 --> 00:21:23.220
This is the president of M.B.I., Minaka Hiroto.

00:21:23.540 --> 00:21:27.710
To all the Ashikabi I'm sending this message to: I've got an important announcement to make.

00:21:28.340 --> 00:21:35.180
In order to make this game somewhat more interesting, I've decided to implement a new rule.

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:41.100
There are already Ashikabi among you who stand no chance of winning, and thus are planning on dropping out.

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:47.060
All the Sekirei in possession of these individuals shall hereby cease to function!

